# inittab(5)

## NAME

inittab - what init starts at boot

## SYNOPSIS

    /etc/inittab

## DESCRIPTION

One entry per line. Words are separated by spaces or tabs; there is no quoting. Lines starting with `#` and empty lines are ignored. A path must be absolute.

## ENTRIES

- `env NAME=VALUE`: set an environment variable for every program (a later line for the same name wins)
- `run PATH [ARGS...]`: run at boot, waiting for each to finish
- `daemon PATH [ARGS...]`: start once in the background
- `respawn PATH [ARGS...]`: start in the background and restart it when it ends
- `shell PATH [ARGS...]`: the console shell (only one)

## EXAMPLES

Show manual pages in Japanese by default:

    env LANG=ja_JP.UTF-8

## SEE ALSO

init(8), man(1)
